From eb124fe8ccad3156655e34b7f9a4bc1e9863ad89 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Andrew Branch <andrewbranch@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 13 Oct 2026 17:59:02 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 6/6] Poll for sync API messages briefly before blocking

Most synchronous API round trips are dominated by the scheduler wakeup latency
of blocking pipe reads rather than by the work done on either side. The sync
client now polls its non-blocking stdout pipe for up to
responsePollMicroseconds (default 100) before switching back to a blocking
read. The server can likewise poll for the next request when the client sets
serverRequestPollMicroseconds (--requestPollMicroseconds, default 0), at a
larger CPU cost since it polls while the client works between requests.

Co-authored-by: Copilot <223556219+Copilot@users.noreply.github.com>
